[TEST] MRI of the symptomatic knee (sagittal T1, T2, and STIR sequences) to evaluate for:  
- Bone marrow edema in the medial proximal tibia or tibial plateau;  
- Signal abnormality or thickening of the pes anserinus tendons;  
- Joint effusion, cartilage defects, or meniscal pathology;  
- Soft-tissue inflammation or bursal enhancement.

